@@ -316,6 +316,31 @@ All operations involving any chip access (probe/read/write/...) require the ``-p
         Be careful, if the provided data doesn't actually match the flash contents, results are undefined.
 
 
+**--ignore-size**
+        Used together with **-w** or **-v**: accept an image file that is smaller than the flash chip instead
+        of failing with "Image size doesn't match the expected size". Only the first *<image size>* bytes of
+        the flash are written or verified, starting at offset 0; the rest of the chip is left untouched
+        (erase blocks that are only partially covered are restored to their previous contents).
+        Images larger than the flash chip are still rejected.
+
+        This option creates its own layout internally and can not be combined with **-l**, **--ifd**,
+        **--fmap**, **--fmap-file** or **-i**. Example::
+
+                flashrom -p mproi_spi --ignore-size -w bootloader.bin
+
+
+**--read-size <size>**
+        Used together with **-r**: read only the first **<size>** bytes of the flash chip (starting at offset 0)
+        and write a file of exactly that size, instead of reading the whole chip. **<size>** may be given in
+        decimal, in hexadecimal with a ``0x`` prefix, or with a ``K`` (KiB) or ``M`` (MiB) suffix. It must not be
+        larger than the flash chip.
+
+        Like **--ignore-size**, this option can not be combined with **-l**, **--ifd**, **--fmap**,
+        **--fmap-file** or **-i**. Example::
+
+                flashrom -p mproi_spi --read-size 64K -r head.bin
+
+
 **-L, --list-supported**
         List the flash chips, chipsets, mainboards, and external programmers (including PCI, USB, parallel port, and serial port based devices)
         supported by **flashrom**.
